{"availability":"available","full":"SchulteDev/multi-resolution-timeseries-parquet","name":"multi-resolution-timeseries-parquet","description":"Years of high-frequency time-series in a browser chart — static Parquet tiers, no backend","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-13T10:35:46Z","updated":"2026-10-13T19:31:04Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://schultedev.github.io/multi-resolution-timeseries-parquet/","topics":["demo","npm","parquet","serverless","vite","vitest"],"demo":"https://schultedev.github.io/multi-resolution-timeseries-parquet/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:00:42.730Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T17:00:42.730Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T17:00:42.730Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T03:23:40.702Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-15T17:00:42.730Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Serve years of high-frequency time-series to a browser chart — no backend, no database. Multi-resolution Parquet tiers + HTTP range requests.","5 years of 1-minute OHLC bars = 2.6M rows = a 105 MB CSV. Parquet skips row groups and projects columns, but it cannot aggregate: \"weekly candles\" is a GROUP BY, which needs a query engine and still scans every underlying row.","So aggregation happens at write time. Precompute tiers at fixed resolutions; the frontend reads only the tier, rows and columns currently in view."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SchulteDev/multi-resolution-timeseries-parquet/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c81978e2181e275e4187d6f17a2848cf9ce8419e973748185119b7e8abf1e13a","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T03:23:40.813Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:23:40.813Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Serve years of high-frequency time-series to a browser chart — no backend, no database. Multi-resolution Parquet tiers + HTTP range requests.","sourceUrl":"https://gith